    "findings": [
      "Nwj: six of seven bDOM interior points are 40.83\u201342.94m NHN with DGM37.29\u201337.37m, far below old53.887\u201357.248m roofs. Seventh48.89m may be vegetation; source has no classification proving a roof. Low-building correction is a promising candidate, not a complete replacement roof survey.",
      "Lb6: bDOM43.18\u201353.33m with DGM37.71\u201337.74m is scattered and not a consistent roof plane. Do not infer uniform lowering.",
      "bDOM measures upper surfaces including vegetation. Acquisition date is not established by the response timestamp. Neither seven points nor one ground plane establish roof slopes, whole footprint currency, demolition or the complete2026aviary boundary.",
      "Both complete original LoD2 parents and current rendered geometry remain unchanged. No large data download, test suite or build was run for this audit."
    ],
    "decision": "Retain both roof profiles unchanged until independent matched roof evidence establishes their shape; fix only the independently reproduced native wolf pose."
  },
